title Soundcheck: the three demo songs saved and made into a set, then soundchecked Muted: each song opened cold, its busiest part played, its change into the next timed, and each song's line kept in the set
covers soundcheck
needs demo-songs
# Live shows B2b: Soundcheck's own lines (show: soundcheck kept song N
# (name): opens in ... · MB · CPU ...; longest disk wait ..., change ...)
# are what it measured on this MPC; devtest_report.py's Soundcheck section
# lists them. Muted, so nothing leaves the outputs. The
# demo songs are put in the run's own library (RAM only on the MPC) and
# saved once each, so their kits' sounds are files the opens read.
wait 2
mark songs-saved
button BROWSE
# Sets then Projects: the list starts again with its first row picked, so
# the first tap on another song picks it and the second opens it.
tap browser place Sets
tap browser place Projects
tap browser row Night Market
tap browser row Night Market
wait 1
expect project: Night Market opened in
tap header tab Arrange
button SHIFT + BROWSE
wait 1
expect project: saved Night Market
button BROWSE
tap browser place Sets
tap browser place Projects
tap browser row Tidal Suite
tap browser row Tidal Suite
wait 1
expect project: Tidal Suite opened in
tap header tab Arrange
button SHIFT + BROWSE
wait 1
expect project: saved Tidal Suite
button BROWSE
tap browser place Sets
tap browser place Projects
# Glass Garden is the first row, picked already: one tap opens it.
tap browser row Glass Garden
wait 1
expect project: Glass Garden opened in
tap header tab Arrange
button SHIFT + BROWSE
wait 1
expect project: saved Glass Garden
mark set-made
tap header tab Arrange
button BROWSE
tap browser place Sets
tap browser sets-button New set
tap browser key Char('c')
tap browser key Char('h')
tap browser key Char('e')
tap browser key Char('c')
tap browser key Char('k')
tap browser key Done
wait 0.5
tap browser sets-button Add songs
wait 0.5
tap browser sets-add Add Night Market
tap browser sets-add Add Glass Garden
tap browser sets-add Add Tidal Suite
tap browser sets-button Done
wait 0.5
tap browser sets-back ‹ Check
wait 0.5
mark soundcheck
# Its question: every song, Muted, then Start. About 3 minutes on the MPC:
# each song's busiest part is up to 16 bars (Tidal Suite's at 76 BPM is
# 50 s), and Let it finish rings out for 10 s at most.
tap browser sets-button Soundcheck
wait 0.5
tap browser sets-value Sound ›
tap browser sets-button Start soundcheck
wait 3
expect show: soundcheck of Check.set (3 songs, muted)
expect show: soundcheck opens Night Market cold
wait 60
expect show: soundcheck kept song 1 (Night Market):
wait 60
expect show: soundcheck kept song 2 (Glass Garden):
wait 70
expect show: soundcheck kept song 3 (Tidal Suite):
expect show: soundcheck of Check.set done: 3 songs in
mark soundcheck-done
tap browser sets-button Done
wait 1
